  "slug": "aumentativos-azo-ote-on",
  "titulo": "Augmentative suffixes: -azo, -ote, -ón",
  "subtitulo": "Perrazo, grandote, cabezón, and a golpe with -azo.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "-azo, -ote, -ón make things bigger, often with admiration or scorn: perrazo, grandote, cabezón. -azo also means a blow with something: cabezazo, codazo.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Instead of adding **grande**, Spanish often uses an **augmentative suffix**: **-azo**, **-ote** or **-ón**. It can mean big size, but it often adds a feeling: **admiration** or **scorn**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Suffix",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "-azo, -aza",
              "perro → perrazo, cuerpo → cuerpazo"
            ],
            [
              "-ote, -ota",
              "grande → grandote, palabra → palabrota"
            ],
            [
              "-ón, -ona",
              "cabeza → cabezón, mujer → mujerona"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "They work with nouns, adjectives and some verbs, and they agree in gender and number: **los relámpagos** → **relampagazos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**-azo** has a special use: a **hit** or blow with something: **cabezazo** (headbutt), **codazo** (elbow), **manotazo** (slap), **portazo** (door slam)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**-azo** also means _great, awesome_ (very common in Mexico): **¡qué golazo!**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-ito** shrinks, **-azo** inflates."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mira ese ==perrazo==. Yo no me le acercaría.",
              "en": "Look at that huge dog. I wouldn't go near it."
            },
            {
              "es": "Se compraron una ==casota== de lujo en otra colonia.",
              "en": "They bought a huge luxury house in another neighborhood."
            },
